---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../schema/faqPage';

const meta = {
  title: 'Schedule a Facility Tour | Sunbright Recovery California',
  description:
    'See Sunbright Recovery Center in person. Schedule a private, no-pressure tour of our Northern California nonprofit recovery facility in Red Bluff.',
  primaryKeyword: 'rehab facility tour',
};

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/design-preview' },
  { name: 'Schedule a Tour', url: '/tour' },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Do I need to have a loved one in treatment to tour?',
    answer:
      'Not at all. Families exploring options before a crisis, individuals thinking ahead, and community members curious about the center are all welcome. Tours are open to anyone who wants to see the space in person.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What will I see on the tour?',
    answer:
      'You will walk through the entire finished facility — residential rooms, group therapy spaces, the chapel, outdoor grounds, dining area, and common spaces. A staff member will explain how each part of the center supports the recovery process.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is there any pressure to enroll during the tour?',
    answer:
      'None whatsoever. Our tours are purely informational. We want you to leave feeling informed and at ease — not sold to. You are welcome to ask any question, and you can take as much time as you need.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I schedule a tour?',
    answer:
      'Call us at (530) 528-2342 or send a message through our contact page. We will find a time that works for you, typically within a few days.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can families and individuals tour together?',
    answer:
      'Yes. We encourage families to come together when possible — seeing the space as a family often makes it easier to have honest conversations about next steps. We are happy to accommodate groups.',
  },
];

const schema = [faqPageSchema(faqs)];
---

<SiteLayout {...meta} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} schema={schema}>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="wrap ph-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Tour Sunbright</span>
      <h1>Come see the center <em>in person.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">Sunbright Recovery Center is a finished, purpose-built facility in Red Bluff, California — and you are welcome to walk through it. No obligation, no pressure. Just an honest look at where recovery happens.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a href="tel:+15305282342" class="btn btn-gold">Call to Schedule — (530) 528-2342</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-ghost">Send a Message</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="prose wide">
        <p>For many people, choosing a recovery center is one of the most important decisions they will ever make. We believe you should be able to look a place in the eye before you trust it with your life — or the life of someone you love.</p>
        <p>Our facility is calm, clean, and built specifically for the work of recovery. Walking through it gives you a feel for the environment, the rhythm of daily life, and the people who make care happen here. It also gives you a chance to ask every question on your mind in a real conversation, not a brochure.</p>

        <h2>What to expect on your visit</h2>
        <p>Every tour is private and led by a staff member who knows the center well. You will see:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Residential rooms</strong> — comfortable, private spaces designed for rest and reflection.</li>
          <li><strong>Group therapy rooms</strong> — where individual and group sessions take place daily.</li>
          <li><strong>Chapel and quiet spaces</strong> — for spiritual reflection, available to all, required of none.</li>
          <li><strong>Dining and common areas</strong> — where community is built over shared meals and conversation.</li>
          <li><strong>Outdoor grounds</strong> — Northern California landscape that supports the healing process.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>At the end of the tour, we set aside time to answer your questions about <a href="/programs/residential">programs</a>, <a href="/admissions">admissions</a>, costs, and anything else on your mind.</p>

        <h2>Who should come</h2>
        <p>Tours are open to individuals considering treatment for themselves, family members exploring options for a loved one, and community supporters who want to see the center firsthand. You do not need to be in crisis or have a decision made — many of our best conversations happen with people who are just beginning to think about the possibilities.</p>

        <div class="callout">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <p><strong>Tours are private and confidential.</strong> We will never share that you visited or contacted us. Your conversation with our team stays between us — from the first call to the last question on the tour.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Ready to schedule?</h2>
        <p>Call us at <a href="tel:+15305282342">(530) 528-2342</a> to set up a time, or <a href="/contact">send a message</a> and we will get back to you within one business day. Tours are available most weekdays and some weekends — we will find a time that works for you.</p>
        <p>If you are ready to talk about next steps beyond a tour, you can also learn about <a href="/admissions">how admissions works</a> or browse our <a href="/programs/residential">residential program</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="aside">
        <h3>Tour at a glance</h3>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          Private, no-pressure visit
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          Staff-led, questions welcome
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          Open to individuals &amp; families
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          Finished, purpose-built facility
        </div>
        <div class="aside-row">
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          Red Bluff, CA — serving Northern California
        </div>
        <a href="tel:+15305282342" class="btn btn-gold">Call (530) 528-2342</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-navy" style="margin-top:10px">Send a Message</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--cream section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Why visit in person</span>
        <h2>A building tells you things <em>a website can't.</em></h2>
        <p class="lead">You will know within minutes whether this is a place where healing can happen. We want you to trust your own read of the space.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"/><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.458 12C3.732 7.943 7.523 5 12 5c4.478 0 8.268 2.943 9.542 7-1.274 4.057-5.064 7-9.542 7-4.477 0-8.268-2.943-9.542-7z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>See the whole center</h3>
          <p>Walk every room, from residential quarters to group spaces to the grounds. No staged showrooms — you see the real facility.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 10h.01M12 10h.01M16 10h.01M9 16H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h14a2 2 0 012 2v8a2 2 0 01-2 2h-5l-5 5v-5z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Ask real questions</h3>
          <p>Talk directly with staff about programs, daily structure, faith integration, costs, and anything else on your mind. Honest answers, every time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.318 6.318a4.5 4.5 0 000 6.364L12 20.364l7.682-7.682a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364-6.364L12 7.636l-1.318-1.318a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364 0z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Feel the environment</h3>
          <p>Recovery happens in a place. Touring lets you trust your gut about whether this environment feels safe, calm, and right for you or your loved one.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</span>
        <h2>Questions about <em>touring</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <div class="faq-body">{faq.answer}</div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <span class="eyebrow">Schedule your visit</span>
    <h2>The door is open. <em>Come see us.</em></h2>
    <p>Call to set up a private tour, or send a message and we will reach out within one business day. No pressure, no commitment — just an honest conversation and a look at a place built for recovery.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a href="tel:+15305282342" class="btn btn-gold">Call (530) 528-2342</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-ghost">Send a Message</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
